## Path:        System/Logging
## Description: go-syslog-view read-only MCP server
## Type:        string
## Default:     "-token-file /etc/go-syslog-view/token"
#
# Command line flags for go-syslog-view. Run "go-syslog-view -h" for all flags.
# Defaults: -listen :8514 -dir /var/log/go-syslog
# The MCP endpoint is http://<host>:8514/mcp (plain HTTP, no TLS).
#
# The package creates a random bearer token in /etc/go-syslog-view/token on
# first install. Clients send it as "Authorization: Bearer <token>".
# Remove -token-file to turn authentication off (anyone who can reach the
# port can then read all logs).
#
# Example: GO_SYSLOG_VIEW_ARGS="-listen 192.168.21.12:8514 -token-file /etc/go-syslog-view/token"
GO_SYSLOG_VIEW_ARGS="-token-file /etc/go-syslog-view/token"
